Subject: [PATCH] firewall4: isolate SYN flood rate limits by ingress interface

The input hook sends new TCP connections from every zone through one shared
token bucket. A burst of SYNs on WAN can therefore consume the entire allowance
before LAN management connections reach their zone's input rules. SSH, HTTP and
SMB then time out while ICMP and established/forwarded traffic continue working.

Key the existing rate limiter by input interface name. Each interface retains
the configured rate and burst, and excess SYNs still reach the existing drop
rule. Limit the dynamic set size, without expiring active limiter state or
changing zone policy. Interface names also avoid accumulating entries when a
PPPoE interface is recreated with a new ifindex.

Destroy the old meter on every ruleset load, including when SYN flood protection
is disabled. Flushing table rules leaves named set elements intact, including
their old rate/burst state. Recreate the meter only when the limiter is enabled,
so configuration changes take effect and disabling protection leaves no stale
set behind. The destroy command also succeeds when the set does not yet exist.

Update the existing ruleset fixtures to expect unconditional meter cleanup.

--- a/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/ruleset.uc
+++ b/root/usr/share/firewall4/templates/ruleset.uc
@@ -7,6 +7,7 @@
 
 table inet fw4
 flush table inet fw4
+destroy set inet fw4 syn_flood_ifaces
 {% if (fw4.check_flowtable()): %}
 delete flowtable inet fw4 ft
 {% endif %}
@@ -212,8 +213,9 @@ table inet fw4 {
 	let b = fw4.default_option("synflood_burst");
 %}
 	chain syn_flood {
-		limit rate {{ r.rate }}/{{ r.unit }}
-		{%- if (b): %} burst {{ b }} packets{% endif %} return comment "!fw4: Accept SYN packets below rate-limit"
+		# Keep WAN SYN bursts from consuming another interface's allowance.
+		meter syn_flood_ifaces size 1024 { meta iifname limit rate {{ r.rate }}/{{ r.unit }}
+		{%- if (b): %} burst {{ b }} packets{% endif %} } return comment "!fw4: Accept SYN packets below per-interface rate-limit"
 		drop comment "!fw4: Drop excess packets"
 	}
 
